server: Don't count an exiting thread of the desktop owner as still running.

The server closes a desktop one second after the process that owns the
desktop window (explorer.exe /desktop) is its only user left. It decides by
comparing the number of threads using the desktop with the owner's running
threads. When one of the owner's own threads exits, kill_thread() releases
the thread's desktop before remove_process_thread() decrements
running_threads, so the exiting thread is still counted and one thread of
another process on the desktop looks like none.

On WinCraft the shell (wcshell.exe) has a single thread. About six seconds
after the last File Explorer window was closed, a worker thread of the
desktop process exited, the server posted WM_CLOSE to the desktop window
and explorer.exe /desktop quit while the shell was still using the desktop.
A wineserver built with logging recorded "users=5, owner running_threads=5"
at that moment. With this change the desktop stays, and it still closes
once the owner is really alone on it.

Status: not for WineHQ as it stands. This patch was written with an LLM,
and WineHQ does not accept LLM-generated code. As of 2026-10-14 no WineHQ
bug or merge request covers this case; bug 59393 reports the same check
closing explorer.exe for another reason.
---
--- a/server/winstation.c
+++ b/server/winstation.c
@@ -417,12 +417,20 @@
 static void remove_desktop_user( struct desktop *desktop, struct thread *thread )
 {
     struct process *process;
+    int owner_threads = 0;
 
     assert( desktop->users > 0 );
     desktop->users--;
 
+    if ((process = get_top_window_owner( desktop )))
+    {
+        owner_threads = process->running_threads;
+        /* an exiting thread of the owner is still counted as running at this point */
+        if (thread->process == process && thread->state == TERMINATED) owner_threads--;
+    }
+
     /* if we have one remaining user, it has to be the manager of the desktop window */
-    if ((process = get_top_window_owner( desktop )) && desktop->users == process->running_threads && !desktop->close_timeout)
+    if (process && desktop->users == owner_threads && !desktop->close_timeout)
         desktop->close_timeout = add_timeout_user( -TICKS_PER_SEC, close_desktop_timeout, desktop );
 }
 
